  "question": {
    "text": "Two bodies of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> are connected to a vertical spring, as shown in the figure. The smaller mass executes simple harmonic motion of angular frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, and amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> while the bigger mass remains stationary on the ground. The maximum force exerted by the system on the floor is (take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>).<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0139_dc180ab4af9d.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 228px;\" />"
  },
